First post! Thanks for stopping by. Before the case studies and deep dives,
here’s a quick tour of what powers this site.

Next.js runs the App Router, with server components, file-based routes, and
ISR refreshing pages about every hour. Contentful handles content: headless
CMS, GraphQL, Rich Text, draft preview, and a CDN for assets. Tailwind CSS
covers styling, with the typography plugin for post bodies, and Inter loads
through next/font. Next/Image resizes and serves images through a small
Contentful loader. TypeScript and pnpm keep types honest and installs fast,
PostCSS and Autoprefixer handle the CSS, and mise pins the Node and pnpm
versions. Vercel does the deploys.

Why this stack? It’s fast, low-maintenance, and built for content: I get a
friendly editing UI in Contentful, and readers get quick pages with solid SEO.

What’s next: more posts, more on the services I offer, better analytics, and
a few interactive bits. If you’re curious how something here works, ask me.
And if you want something like this for your company, say hello.
